      <publication_year>2021</publication_year>
      <description>Numerical shape model of asteroid 243 Ida, constructed from Galileo images of Ida
taken August 28, 1993, using stereogrammetry and limb matching techniques. This shape
model consists of a grid with points every 2 degrees in latitude and longitude, with
a radius in km associated with each point.  Longitudes are East. Coordinates are
planetocentric. Spin pole: RA = 348.76 +/- 7.5, Dec = 87.10 +/- 0.4 (degrees) J2000;
rotation period = 0.1930680 days Retrograde.  Prime meridian: W = 265.95
1864.6280070d (degrees)  where d is the number of days from the standard epoch (JD
2451545.0).</description>
    </Citation_Information>
